WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.096
Your calendar makes room for meetings. Dayweave makes room for your routines,

2
00:00:05.096 --> 00:00:11.900
connecting Gmail, Google Calendar and Google Sheets. This walkthrough uses synthetic data.

3
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.959
Coffee timing uses timestamped purchases when there is enough history.

4
00:00:15.959 --> 00:00:23.667
A purchase does not prove consumption, and email delivery time never substitutes for purchase time.

5
00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:28.927
Sleep timing works backward from your chosen target, morning preparation and first commitment.

6
00:00:28.927 --> 00:00:35.533
You can inspect the assumptions. This is scheduling, not a health prediction.

7
00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:37.802
Meetings overlap the preferred lunch time.

8
00:00:37.802 --> 00:00:44.200
Dayweave finds a complete opening around those commitments and shows why it fits.

9
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:49.794
Gemini actually ran on synthetic observations, calling read-only tools to select a focus.

10
00:00:49.794 --> 00:00:56.700
Validated scheduling rules own the times. The activity trace shows the work.

11
00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.335
I choose an action and review its exact event details and Sheets operation.

12
00:01:01.335 --> 00:01:05.633
Nothing is written until I explicitly confirm.

13
00:01:05.633 --> 00:01:08.393
The approved event appears in the schedule.

14
00:01:08.393 --> 00:01:14.333
These walkthrough changes are simulated. The result clearly reports what happened.

15
00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:20.138
Activity records the action. Repeated approval does not create duplicate events or rows.

16
00:01:20.138 --> 00:01:25.067
The live provider rechecks availability before insertion.

17
00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:29.765
With sparse history, Dayweave uses your preference instead of inventing a habit.

18
00:01:29.765 --> 00:01:33.933
Every suggestion remains yours to choose.

19
00:01:33.933 --> 00:01:37.943
Separately, live Gmail and Calendar reads, a Sheets preference save,

20
00:01:37.943 --> 00:01:46.000
and an approved Calendar lunch with its Sheets log were verified. Repeating it created no duplicate.
